@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@ Bugs
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026` returning one run at another sampling rate: ``sub-09`` ``run-01`` is stored at about 1200 Hz (EDF header 1199.4 Hz) while the other 447 runs of the 45 subjects are at 512 Hz, so any paradigm call including subject 9 stopped in ``np.concatenate`` ("the array at index 0 has size 1281 and the array at index 2 has size 3000"). The loader now resamples any run that is not at 512 Hz to 512 Hz after locating its events. Cached ``PerezBlanco2026`` epochs and results of subject 9 must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`1277` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhang2017` no longer guesses channel names for files it was not checked against. Every released file has 17 channels and an empty BCI2000 ``ChannelNames`` parameter (all 180 ``.dat`` files of the 12 subjects, checked) and keeps the EGI sensor order ``E1``-``E16``, ``E28``. Before, a file with another channel count got ``EEG001``.. names and a file with header names got those labels, which would have given its subject a channel set of its own; such files now raise a ``ValueError``. The returned data are unchanged (:gh:`XXXX` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhang2017` no longer guesses channel names for files it was not checked against. Every released file has 17 channels and an empty BCI2000 ``ChannelNames`` parameter (all 180 ``.dat`` files of the 12 subjects, checked) and keeps the EGI sensor order ``E1``-``E16``, ``E28``. Before, a file with another channel count got ``EEG001``.. names and a file with header names got those labels, which would have given its subject a channel set of its own; such files now raise a ``ValueError``. The returned data are unchanged (:gh:`1278` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Fix the Castillos2023 c-VEP loaders (:class:`moabb.datasets.CastillosBurstVEP100`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosBurstVEP40`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosCVEP100`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosCVEP40`) failing for every subject with ``ValueError: The event_id dictionary has values that do not match any event codes ... Missing event codes: [0]``: the trial labels were a view of ``epochs.events``, so making them 0-based also rewrote the epochs' event codes, which MNE now checks when the epochs are read. The labels are now a copy, and all 12 subjects of the four datasets load again (:gh:`XXXX` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Fix the Castillos2023 c-VEP loaders (:class:`moabb.datasets.CastillosBurstVEP100`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosBurstVEP40`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosCVEP100`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.CastillosCVEP40`) failing for every subject with ``ValueError: The event_id dictionary has values that do not match any event codes ... Missing event codes: [0]``: the trial labels were a view of ``epochs.events``, so making them 0-based also rewrote the epochs' event codes, which MNE now checks when the epochs are read. The labels are now a copy, and all 12 subjects of the four datasets load again (:gh:`1279` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2024` no longer loads subjects 5, 15 and 49 by default: their released files are derived from the recordings of subjects 4, 11 and 47 (EDF of sub-05 bit-identical to sub-04; raw MAT files equal to the partner's recording minus uniform noise), while ``participants.tsv`` lists them as different patients, so keeping them leaked one subject's EEG across cross-subject folds. The dataset now exposes 47 subjects; ``include_derived_subjects=True`` restores all 50 released IDs with a warning. Scores computed on all 50 subjects are not comparable with the new default (:gh:`1248` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Follow-ups from the review of :gh:`1257`-:gh:`1270`: :func:`moabb.benchmark` lets the evaluation auto-select datasets when no ``include_datasets``/``exclude_datasets`` is given, so its default run no longer warns about filtered datasets (:gh:`862`), and "No datasets left" now lists the reasons; the weekly scheduled link check no longer accepts 5xx answers, so a host that stays down is reported; the PhysioNet S3 mirror is skipped for the rest of the process after its first failure instead of warning and timing out once per file (:gh:`1245`); a metadata-aware ``cv_class`` now rejects a ``groups`` argument it would silently ignore, and the CrossSession limitation is documented (:gh:`1104`); a Zhou2020 file that does not match the channel layout raises instead of being skipped (:gh:`1120`); the Rozado2015 unit check accepts common spellings of microvolts (:gh:`1070`); ``Lioi2020_XP2.nemar_subject_template`` is read-only and a missing mapping key names the expected key type (:gh:`1098`); the ``process()`` Notes state that saving finished subjects is best effort with ``n_jobs > 1`` (:gh:`419`) (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - With ``optuna=True``, ROC-AUC scoring failed with ``AttributeError: ... has no attribute 'decision_function'`` for classifiers that only provide ``predict_proba`` (skorch/braindecode nets, ``GaussianNB``, ...): optuna-integration's ``OptunaSearchCV`` defines ``decision_function`` unconditionally, so scikit-learn's scorer picked it. ``OptunaSearchCVClassifier`` now exposes it only when the underlying estimator has it, as scikit-learn's ``BaseSearchCV`` does (:gh:`1251` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
